6.2 Identity Integration with Entra Agent ID

PONA's cryptographic identity root I_{\text{crypto}} is orthogonal to Microsoft's Agent ID. The integration is:

\text{Microsoft Agent ID} = \text{transient session identity } (\in X_t)

\text{PONA } I_{\text{crypto}} = \text{persistent cryptographic identity } (\in S_t^{P})

Definition 11 (Identity Binding). The PONA identity root is bound to the Microsoft Agent ID through a signed attestation:

\text{Attest}(I_{\text{crypto}}, \text{AgentID}_{\text{MS}}) = \text{Sign}_{\text{TPM}}(h(I_{\text{crypto}} \parallel \text{AgentID}_{\text{MS}}))

This attestation is stored in the persistent state plane. If the Microsoft Agent ID is deleted and recreated, the PONA identity can re-attest to the new Agent ID, preserving \pi_{I_{\text{crypto}}}(S_t^{P}) = I_{\text{crypto}}.

The attestation mechanism uses TPM quotes verified against Azure Attestation. A TPM quote is a signed assertion over selected PCR values, and Azure Attestation verifies the quote against a policy asserting expected system measurements.

6.3 MCP Proxy Integration with Agent Governance Toolkit

The Agent Governance Toolkit provides four composable layers for MCP governance: a Trust Proxy for authorization, a Trust Server for Ed25519 identity and trust scoring, a Security Scanner for tool poisoning detection, and an MCP Gateway for allow/deny filtering and audit logging. PONA extends this with:

Definition 12 (Provenance Tagging at MCP Proxy). Every MCP tool call carries a provenance tag:

\text{prov}(\text{call}) = (\text{source}, \; \text{trust-level}, \; \text{epistemic-type}, \; \text{timestamp})

The MCP proxy enforces:

\text{trust-level}(\text{prov}(\text{call})) \geq \text{RequiredTrust}(\text{tool})

6.4 Windows ODR Integration

Windows ODR provides a secure, manageable interface for discovering and utilizing agent connectors from local apps and remote servers using MCP. odr.exe is the CLI that enables MCP servers to be listed, registered, and interacted with on Windows. PONA registers its commit protocol handlers as ODR connectors:

```powershell
odr.exe mcp add --name "PONA-Commit-Handler" `
  --command "pona-kernel.exe --commit-protocol" `
  --args "--ledger C:\ProgramData\PONA\ledger --tpm-attestation" `
  --auth "tpm-attestation"
```

